# CAO-OMS line-ending policy.
#
# LF is mandatory in the WORKING TREE, not merely in the object store, for two
# reasons that have both already bitten this repository:
#
#   1. Checksums. release.sh computes SHA-256 of the working-tree oms.html and
#      that value is quoted in the release note, checked by verify_live.sh
#      against the deployed file, and used as the rollback baseline. A CRLF
#      checkout makes every one of those mismatch.
#   2. The tooling is bash. scripts/*.sh under a CRLF checkout fail in Git Bash
#      with a bad-interpreter error, so the release gate cannot even run.
#
# Setting core.autocrlf=false on one clone is not enough: a fresh clone on any
# other machine would still check out CRLF. This file makes the policy travel
# with the repository. See CLAUDE.md, "Running the tooling on Windows".

# Normalise every text file to LF, on checkout and on commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The deployed artifacts. GitHub Pages serves these byte for byte and their
# hashes are quoted in release notes, so they must be identical everywhere.
*.html  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# Executable tooling. CRLF here breaks the shebang in Git Bash.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# Binary. Never convert, never diff as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xlsm  binary
*.zip   binary
